        ],
        "decisions": [
          {
            "topic": "Browser read transport",
            "choice": "Reject the Server-Action-for-reads shortcut and add one GET Route Handler at app/api/labels/route.ts",
            "rationale": "The task requires cacheable HTTP GET browser reads. Server Actions are POSTs, are queued sequentially per client, and return an action payload, so they cannot be HTTP-cached under any configuration. This is a runtime requirement, not a stylistic preference, and it costs exactly one file."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Security shortcut",
            "choice": "Reject \"middleware and RLS already cover security\"; authenticate in all three channels, recheck permission in server.ts, keep explicit ownership predicates in the store",
            "rationale": "Middleware, layouts, and hidden UI do not authorize data, and each Server Action is a public HTTP entrypoint. RLS is the last line, not the only one. Enforcement runs at channel, capability policy, and store boundaries."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Application layer and ports",
            "choice": "Accept the shortcut: no application/ segment, no repository port, no forwarding operation",
            "rationale": "Deleting an operation here would move nothing into callers. Input parsing, auth, row mapping, cache invalidation, and an ordinary unique-name conflict do not qualify, and Supabase is the only planned provider, so a port would name no technology-independent need."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Capability boundary",
            "choice": "One module, src/modules/labels/, covering the page read, HTTP read, and both mutations",
            "rationale": "One product goal, one vocabulary, one lifecycle, one change authority. A page, a table, or a CRUD surface does not create a capability, and file count is not a boundary criterion."
          },
          {
            "topic": "Public surfaces",
            "choice": "server.ts, actions.ts, client.ts only; no rsc.ts, no ui.ts, no query-cache.ts",
